  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\n     The central idea is to use a genetic algorithm (GA) to explore the solution space more thoroughly and escape local optima found by gradient-based methods. The objective function measures the maximum correlation between h(x) and (1-h(x+k)) for shifts k. Since the function is non-convex, a GA with crossover, mutation, and elitism is better suited to finding a global minimum. This approach starts from parents if available for faster convergence but deploys multiple GA processes concurrently to explore different underlying patterns.\n\n  2. Mathematical Specification:\n     - Representation: A function h(x) is represented as a dense vector of length N_points (fixed at 200).\n     - Objective: C5(h) = max_k \u222b h(x) * (1 - h(x+k)) dx = (2.0 / N_points) * max_lag(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")[lag])\n     - Constraints: \u2211h[i] = N_points/2 and 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i.\n     - Projection: After mutation/crossover, individuals are projected using a Levenberg-Marquardt method to maintain sum constraint (0.1% tolerance).\n\n  3. Implementation Procedure:\n     1. Initialize population (N_GA=100 individuals) from parent (if given) and/or random samples.\n     2. Evolution Loop (until time budget 1100s < 1:58:04):\n        a. Selection: Tournament selection (size 5) per parent\n        b. Crossover: Single-point crossover (probability 0.8)\n        c. Mutation: Gaussian mutation (mean \u03bc=ind_val, std \u03c3=0.1) with bounds projection\n        d. Replace worst individuals with GA progeny\n        e. Local Search: Run Nesterov subgradient (N_iter=40) on best individual for hyperparameter tuning\n        f. Check sum constraint and clip values\n        g. Time tracking: Break loop if time exceeds budget\n     3. Final Output: Best candidate and its C5 score\n\n  4. Search Choices:\n     - Population Size: 50 initial, expand to 150 if time remains\n     - Mutation: Normal noise (std=0.05)\n     - Crossover: Single-point (probability 0.9)\n     - Elitism: Retain top 10% of population\n     - Local Search: Run SLSQP on top 1% with beta=500\n     - Time Budgets: Allocate 70% GA, 30% optimization refinement\n\n  5. Compute Budget and Robustness:\n     - Dominant cost: O(N_points * N_GA * N_iters) per generation.\n     - Estimated time per generation: 0.2-0.5s at N_points=200.\n     - Monitor time usage periodically: Break after 8000 generations (max \u223c500s).\n     - Fallback: Return parent solution if GA fails.\n\n  6. Validation and Return Contract:\n     - Return (h_final, C5_final, 200) tuple\n     - Verify: \u2211h_final = 100, all 0\u2264h_final[i]\u22641\n     - Re-evaluate final candidate via compute_c5()",
